# Template for your private settings file. It lists every setting the app reads, with empty values.
# Used by: the Python server in backend/ (it reads all of these) and the Vite client in frontend/
# (it reads only the VITE_ ones).
#
# How to use it: copy this file to .env in the repository root, next to this file, and fill in
# the values on your own machine.
#   cp .env.example .env
# The server reads it with: uv run --env-file ../.env (see docs/ENGINEERING.md, section 3).
# Never put real values in this file. Never commit .env. On Vercel, enter the same names in
# Project Settings, Environment Variables.
#
# Tags used below:
#   [safe for browser] = not secret. It is fine if it ends up in browser code.
#   [SERVER ONLY]      = secret. Never in browser code, never in a VITE_ variable, never in Git,
#                        never in a chat message or a coding agent prompt.

# [safe for browser] Which copy of the app this is: local, preview or production. Empty means local.
APP_ENV=

# [safe for browser] Web address of our Supabase project, like https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# [safe for browser] Supabase publishable key. Row-level security in the database protects the data.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# [SERVER ONLY] Supabase secret key. It skips row-level security, so only the server may hold it.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# [SERVER ONLY] Password for the daily keep-alive route (GET /api/keepalive). The daily GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/keepalive.yml) sends it as "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>", from the repository secret CRON_SECRET, which holds the same value. The name dates from the time we planned to use Vercel Cron, which we cannot use. Use a long random string. Empty on your laptop is fine: the route then answers 503 not_configured.
CRON_SECRET=

# [safe for browser] true or false. true = demo mode, for showing the game without real outside services. Empty means false. In demo mode the Island Exchange plays a public recording of island prices (stocks are not part of it and are hidden) and never calls Binance or the stock provider: fine for a demo or a rehearsal, but those prices can be read in advance, so coins won on them must not count for anything real. Every deployment that shares one database should use the same value.
DEMO_MODE=

# [safe for browser] Feature flags to switch on, comma separated. Names: market, predictions, sports, arena, raid, live_presence, companion_llm. Not listed means off. A typo stops the server.
FEATURE_FLAGS=

# [safe for browser] Name of the place whose real weather the game shows (live weather from Open-Meteo, which needs no key). Shown on screen, at most 60 characters. Empty means the default: Torshavn, Faroe Islands. The default is the team's proposal and may change.
WEATHER_PLACE_NAME=

# [safe for browser] Latitude of that place in degrees, from -90 to 90, written with a dot like 62.01. Empty means the default (62.01, the Faroe Islands). For Lisbon use 38.72.
WEATHER_LATITUDE=

# [safe for browser] Longitude of that place in degrees, from -180 to 180, written with a dot like -6.77. Empty means the default (-6.77, the Faroe Islands). For Lisbon use -9.14. A wrong value stops the server at start-up with a clear message.
WEATHER_LONGITUDE=

# [safe for browser] Island Exchange: which stock-price provider shows the prices of its real stock companies (Apple, NVIDIA, Tesla, Coca-Cola, Spotify). Empty means off, and then the Exchange lists only the island companies. Today the only name is: finnhub. Anything else stops the server at start-up. Set it only when a teammate has created the key below AND Finnhub has agreed in writing that the prices may be shown to the players (docs/DECISIONS.md, D017). The server never calls the provider in demo mode.
STOCK_API_PROVIDER=

# [SERVER ONLY] The key of that stock-price provider (a free Finnhub key). A teammate creates it; an agent never signs up for it. It lives only in the Vercel settings and your private .env, never in the browser, a log or the repository. The server sends it in a request header and never writes it to a log. Empty keeps the stocks off (the server logs one warning if a provider is named without a key).
STOCK_API_KEY=

# [safe for browser] Copy of SUPABASE_URL for the Vite client. Vite only passes VITE_ variables to the browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# [safe for browser] Copy of SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY for the Vite client.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Keys for later features. Not used yet. Each one is a secret: remove the leading # only when its feature is built.

# [SERVER ONLY] NOT USED. The Island Exchange (feature flag: market) reads Binance market data, which needs no key. This line is kept for a later CoinGecko backup: a teammate would have to create that free key (an agent never signs up), and it would live only in Vercel (docs/INTERFACES.md, section 9).
# MARKET_DATA_API_KEY=

# [SERVER ONLY] Key for the sports results service (feature flag: sports).
# SPORTS_API_KEY=

# [SERVER ONLY] Key for the language model behind the companion (feature flag: companion_llm).
# LLM_API_KEY=
